course: dictionary
lesson: 4501
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives hawk four meanings: a bird, a way of selling, a noisy throat-clearing, and a warlike person. Context helps you choose the right one.
explain: «Owls, foxes, cats, weasels, snakes and hawks all hunt mice.» Hunt is the clue here. Animals hunt, so hawk must mean the bird. Ask yourself: what word would fit in this sentence, and does your meaning still make sense?
explain: «At the bird of prey show... a hawk comes back to the glove because it has learned the glove means food.» Glove and food are the clues. Here hawk is still the bird, which shows that a word's meaning can be the same across different sentences.
explain: Some words change meaning with a little help. «Street sellers hawked goods» means they walked about calling out to sell things. A hawk in the sky and a hawker at a market share one word but do different jobs. Clues like «goods» and «street» tell you which meaning to use.
fact: A hawk is a bird of prey with sharp eyes, a hooked beak and strong claws called talons.
fact: Hawks hunt small animals and sit at the top of a food chain.
fact: «Falcons look like hawks, but they are closer cousins of parrots and songbirds.»
fact: To hawk can mean to sell things by walking about and calling out, like at a market.
fact: «Eyes like a hawk» means having very sharp eyesight, and «watch someone like a hawk» means to watch them very closely.
exercise: «Owls, foxes, cats, weasels, snakes and hawks all hunt mice.» In this sentence, what is a hawk? | A small furry mammal | A kind of street seller | *A bird of prey that hunts small animals | A person who loves peace
exercise: Dad says, «Let's hawk these old books at the car boot sale.» What does hawk mean here? | *To sell things by walking about and calling out | To clear your throat noisily | To hide the books | To fly high over the hills
exercise: «Mum watched the baby like a hawk.» What does this phrase mean? | *Mum watched the baby very closely | Mum watched the baby while sleeping | Mum flew above the baby | Mum was hungry and wanted food
test: «The farmer heard a hawk screech above the field, then saw it dive for a mouse.» Which meaning of hawk is used? | To sell things at a market | *A bird of prey | A person who prefers warlike actions | To clear your throat noisily
test: Ella hears her brother hawk loudly before he speaks. Which meaning fits? | *To clear your throat noisily | A warlike person who wants a fight | A bird with sharp claws | To sell goods in the street
exam: Which sentence uses hawk to mean a warlike person who prefers strong actions? | He had to hawk his old bike | *The general was a hawk who wanted war, not peace | The hawk circled over the lake | The baby watched the hawk through the window
